      "content": "These profound feelings of detachment and numbness can be incredibly frightening and isolating. What you're describing might be a form of emotional dissociation, which is a protective response when we face something too immense to process. It does not define your entire being; it is a symptom of a deeply distressing event. Speaking with a mental health professional can help explore these sensations and understand what your mind is doing to protect you right now.",
      "source": "target",
